cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this reproducibility package, please cite the archived software record and the associated manuscript."
title: "Positive Approximation under Subspace Decoupling: From Frobenius to Spectral Norm: reproducibility package"
type: software
version: "1.0.1-submission"
date-released: 2026-08-11
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/xin-lu-creator/positive-approximation-reproducibility"
authors:
  - family-names: Lu
    given-names: Xin
    affiliation: Iwate University
abstract: >-
  Deterministic verification code and exact-rational certificate files for the
  manuscript "Positive Approximation under Subspace Decoupling: From Frobenius to Spectral Norm". The package verifies the explicit Schatten
  counterexample constructions and the certified rational 4 x 4 obstruction
  for rank-(1,1) spectral-norm certificates. No external dataset or randomness
  is required.
keywords:
  - positive semidefinite approximation
  - spectral norm
  - Schatten norm
  - matrix nearness
  - semidefinite programming
  - exact rational verification
